WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.707
We will start with ordinary CTEs because they make complex queries easier to read.

00:00:04.707 --> 00:00:08.307
Then we will introduce recursive CTEs for hierarchies.

00:00:08.307 --> 00:00:11.807
After that, we will study the OVER clause and window functions.

00:00:11.807 --> 00:00:14.387
Ranking and sequence functions come next.

00:00:14.387 --> 00:00:16.587
Then we will make frames explicit.

00:00:16.587 --> 00:00:21.257
Finally, we will combine CTEs and windows into useful analytical patterns.

00:00:21.257 --> 00:00:24.557
Keep a real project in mind as we work through this section—for example,

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:28.802
a hospital ranking visits and identifying readmissions.

00:00:28.802 --> 00:00:33.062
The technical feature matters because it changes what questions we can answer reliably and how easily another

00:00:33.062 --> 00:00:36.112
analyst can understand our work.

00:00:36.112 --> 00:00:41.667
As you listen, try to connect each SQL or data concept to a decision you might need to defend later:

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:45.787
what the data means, what one row represents, what can be missing,

00:00:45.787 --> 00:00:48.240
and what assumptions the transformation introduces.
